(7701872, 1264216, 141319, '<td valign="top">Lovely picture Roz, congratulations.<br/>Have you tried making rain by using a layer of "noise" and giving it a motion blur?<br/>The direction of the drops is then constant (your brush doesn''t seem to always be in the same direction?), and the drops are more random. But you then have to play with layers and blur some of them, else it looks fake :-)</td>', 'Lovely picture Roz, congratulations.Have you tried making rain by using a layer of "noise" and giving it a motion blur?The direction of the drops is then constant (your brush doesn''t seem to always be in the same direction?), and the drops are more random. But you then have to play with layers and blur some of them, else it looks fake :-)', '2021-09-23 02:42:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(7701873, 1264245, 141319, '<td valign="top">What a great capture!</td>', 'What a great capture!', '2021-09-23 02:43:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(7701874, 1264022, 141319, '<td valign="top">Stunning - I am going on a photo trip next week and one of the "lessons" will be astro photography - can''t wait to learn this.</td>', 'Stunning - I am going on a photo trip next week and one of the "lessons" will be astro photography - can''t wait to learn this.', '2021-09-23 02:44:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(7701875, 1264235, 141319, '<td valign="top">What a great "picture". Love the story and innuendo you can read into this.</td>', 'What a great "picture". Love the story and innuendo you can read into this.', '2021-09-23 02:46:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7701878, 1264216, 67145, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kasaba:</b></div><hr/><i> Lovely picture Roz, congratulations.<br/>Have you tried making rain by using a layer of "noise" and giving it a motion blur?<br/>The direction of the drops is then constant (your brush doesn''t seem to always be in the same direction?), and the drops are more random. But you then have to play with layers and blur some of them, else it looks fake :-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>thankyou so much Gaby .. I will definately look into that xx</td>', 'Originally posted by kasaba: Lovely picture Roz, congratulations.Have you tried making rain by using a layer of "noise" and giving it a motion blur?The direction of the drops is then constant (your brush doesn''t seem to always be in the same direction?), and the drops are more random. But you then have to play with layers and blur some of them, else it looks fake :-)   thankyou so much Gaby .. I will definately look into that xx', '2021-09-23 06:26:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(7701879, 1264255, 117099, '<td valign="top">Beautiful!</td>', 'Beautiful!', '2021-09-23 06:41:41.000000', NULL, 0),
